.\" man page create by R# package system.
.TH FUZZYGENE 1 2000-1月 "fuzzygene_analysis_report" "fuzzygene_analysis_report"
.SH NAME
fuzzygene_analysis_report \- Run every analysis once and write the tables to a folder.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIfuzzygene_analysis_report(\fBfuzzygene\fR as <generic> FuzzyGeneModel, 
\fBgene\fR as string, 
\fBgeneA\fR as string = \fB<NULL>\fR, 
\fBgeneB\fR as string = \fB<NULL>\fR, 
\fBdir\fR as string = \fB<NULL>\fR, 
\fBmode\fR as string = "knockout", 
\fBomegas\fR as double = \fB<NULL>\fR, 
\fBstepsList\fR as double = \fB<NULL>\fR, 
\fBdoses\fR as double = \fB<NULL>\fR, 
\fBsweepSteps\fR as integer = 50, 
\fBdoseSteps\fR as integer = 60, 
\fBcombinationSteps\fR as integer = 60, 
\fBtop\fR as integer = 50, 
\fBsurfaceTop\fR as integer = 20, 
\fBlagRatio\fR as double = 0.1, 
\fBtolerance\fR as double = 0.001, 
[\fB<Environment>\fR]);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Run every analysis once and write the tables to a folder.
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBfuzzygene\fB \fR\- a trained (or restored) model. 
.PP
.PP
\fBgene\fB \fR\- the target gene of the single perturbation analyses. 
.PP
.PP
\fBgeneA\fB \fR\- the first gene of the combination analysis; empty skips that part. 
.PP
.PP
\fBgeneB\fB \fR\- the second gene of the combination analysis; empty skips that part. 
.PP
.PP
\fBdir\fB \fR\- the output folder (created when missing). 
.PP
.PP
\fBmode\fB \fR\- \fBknockout\fR (default), \fBknockdown\fR or \fBoverexpression\fR. 
.PP
.PP
\fBomegas\fB \fR\- relaxation grid; \fBNULL\fR uses \fBc(0.2, 0.5, 0.8, 1.0)\fR. 
.PP
.PP
\fBstepsList\fB \fR\- step grid of the invariance check; \fBNULL\fR uses \fBc(50, 200, 500)\fR. 
.PP
.PP
\fBdoses\fB \fR\- dose grid; \fBNULL\fR uses 5 evenly spaced points. 
.PP
.PP
\fBsweepSteps\fB \fR\- fixed iteration budget of the omega / lag analyses. 
.PP
.PP
\fBdoseSteps\fB \fR\- iteration budget of the dose analyses. 
.PP
.PP
\fBcombinationSteps\fB \fR\- iteration budget of the combination analysis. 
.PP
.PP
\fBtop\fB \fR\- number of genes kept in the dose and combination tables. 
.PP
.PP
\fBsurfaceTop\fB \fR\- number of genes kept in the dose-time surface. 
.PP
.PP
\fBlagRatio\fB \fR\- relative trigger threshold of the lag definition. 
.PP
.PP
\fBtolerance\fB \fR\- relative deviation threshold of the invariant flags. 
.PP
.PP
\fBenv\fB \fR\- the R# runtime environment used to report errors. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
a character vector of the written file paths
.PP
.SH DETAILS
.PP
Writes into the folder:
 \fBanalysis.sensitivity.csv\fR (omega + step sweeps),
 \fBanalysis.lag.csv\fR, \fBanalysis.spearman.csv\fR,
 \fBanalysis.dose_response.csv\fR, \fBanalysis.dose_time_surface.csv\fR,
 \fBanalysis.combination.csv\fR (when both genes are given) and
 \fBanalysis.report.json\fR (grid definition, invariant flags, run count, elapsed time).
 


 


 This is the cheap way to get everything: calling the four analysis apis separately would
 repeat the dose sweep twice. Expect one to two minutes on an 18k gene model with the
 default grids.
 


 
\fB
 let files = FuzzyGene::fuzzygene_analysis_report(
     model, "TPPP3", geneA = "HSD17B3", geneB = "TPPP3", dir = "/path/analysis");
 print(files);
 
\fR`
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
FuzzyGene
.SH FILES
.PP
biosystem.dll
.PP
